Test Fixtures Directory
=======================

This directory contains sample vendor invoice files for testing the 
invoice extraction and normalization pipeline.

File Naming Convention
----------------------
Name invoice files using the pattern:
    {vendorname}_invoice_{number}.csv

Examples:
    - sysco_invoice_001.csv
    - usfoods_invoice_001.csv
    - examplevendor_invoice_001.csv

Invoice File Format
-------------------
Each invoice should be a CSV file with at minimum these columns:
    - Item (or Product): Product name/description
    - Qty (or Quantity): Quantity ordered
    - Unit Price (or Price): Price per unit

Optional columns:
    - Unit (or UOM): Unit of measure (lb, kg, ea, etc.)
    - Total: Total line item price

Example CSV content:
--------------------
Item,Qty,Unit Price
Chicken Thighs,10,2.50
Ground Beef,5 lbs,4.99
Olive Oil,2,8.99

Adding Test Fixtures
--------------------
1. Obtain a sample invoice from a vendor (or create a test CSV)
2. Convert to CSV format if necessary
3. Ensure it has the required columns (Item, Qty, Unit Price)
4. Name it following the convention above
5. Place it in this directory

Running Tests
-------------
To test the pipeline with your fixtures:

    python scripts/extract_normalize.py \
        --input-dir tests/fixtures \
        --output-dir output \
        --master-products master_products.csv

The output Excel file will be created in the output/ directory.

Notes
-----
- Keep invoice files small for testing purposes
- Sanitize any sensitive vendor pricing data before committing
- You can create subdirectories by vendor if you have many fixtures
